usage: gen_check.py [-h] --repo REPO [--seed SEED] [--examples EXAMPLES]
                    [--expect-fail NAME] [--timeout S] [--call-timeout S]
                    [--json]
                    props

Seeded Python property checks against declared repo targets (stdlib only).
PROPS.py imports combinators and reject from gen_check, defines properties =
{name: (generator, check)}, and TARGETS = ["path.py:Class.method"]. Optional
examples = {name: [inputs]}, setup(), reset(), CHECK_TIMEOUT (seconds for the
run). Hooks run before each input and shrink attempt. Only check(input) is
profiled; rejected and timed-out inputs do not count toward target coverage. A
failure is reduced with at most 500 attempts, not guaranteed minimal. An input
whose hooks and check run past --call-timeout ends its property as timeout;
the other properties still run. During shrinking, a timeout instead keeps the
confirmed failure and marks the reduction incomplete; --expect-fail cannot
pass. Exit 0 pass, 1 property/filter/target failure, 2 usage or infrastructure
error, 3 inconclusive: a call/run limit or Ctrl-C stopped a check and nothing
failed outright. --expect-fail never accepts infrastructure failures or
timeouts. Zero disables the corresponding time limit. While enabled, the
checker reserves SIGALRM; checked code must not use alarm/setitimer.

positional arguments:
  props                PROPS.py with properties and declared TARGETS

options:
  -h, --help           show this help message and exit
  --repo REPO          repository whose functions must run
  --seed SEED          random seed (default: 0)
  --examples EXAMPLES  generated inputs per property after pinned examples
                       (default: 100)
  --expect-fail NAME   exit 0 only for a counterexample to this property
  --timeout S          seconds for the whole run, then exit 3 (overrides
                       PROPS.CHECK_TIMEOUT; default: 90; imports use CLI or
                       90; 0 disables)
  --call-timeout S     seconds for one input's hooks and check, then exit 3
                       (default: 10; 0 disables)
  --json               machine-readable output

