                        model

Breadth-first explicit-state model checker for a Python model (init, actions, invariants). Prints a shortest counterexample trace on violation.

positional arguments:
  model                 the MODEL.py file

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --depth DEPTH         max steps from an initial state (default: MODEL.DEPTH
                        or 25)
  --max-states MAX_STATES
                        stop after this many distinct states (default:
                        MODEL.MAX_STATES or 200000)
  --invariant NAME      check only these invariants (repeatable)
  --deadlock            also fail on states with no enabled action (unless
                        terminal)
  --mutants             also run every MODEL.mutants entry; each must violate
                        an invariant
  --expect-violation NAME
                        succeed only if invariant NAME is violated (able-to-
                        fail proof)
  --timeout S           seconds for the whole run, then exit 3 (overrides
                        MODEL.CHECK_TIMEOUT; default: 90; imports use CLI or
                        90; 0 disables)
  --call-timeout S      seconds for one call to actions(), an invariant, or a
                        mutant, then exit 2 (default: 10; 0 disables)
  --json                machine-readable output

examples:
  bounded_check.py references/example_model.py
  bounded_check.py model.py --depth 30 --deadlock
  bounded_check.py model.py --mutants                 # every broken variant must be caught
  bounded_check.py model.py --expect-violation no_lost_todo   # exit 0 only if it fails

MODEL.py: init() or inits(); actions(state) -> [(name, next_state)]; invariants = {name: fn};
optional terminal(state), describe(state), mutants = {name: actions_fn}, DEPTH, MAX_STATES, CHECK_TIMEOUT.
exit: 0 holds within the bound, 1 violation/deadlock/surviving mutant, 2 model or usage error
(a call to actions(), an invariant, or a mutant past --call-timeout is a model error),
3 stopped at the --timeout run limit: not a failure and not a proof

